---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import groupPhoto from '../assets/pages/2024-08-06.lab-group2.jpg';
---
{/* §5b: "Join us" folds in here rather than competing with Publications for a nav
    slot. /join/ and /contact/ both 301 to this anchor. Prose is carried over from
    the Jekyll join page verbatim — it is the lab's own writing, not placeholder. */}
<section id="join" class="join">
  <h2>Join the team</h2>

  <Image src={groupPhoto} alt="The Talmo Lab group, 2024" width={1400} class="group-photo" />
  <p class="caption muted">The group, ca. 2024. Photo credit: Chris Keeney</p>

  <p>
    Interested in our work? Reach out to <a href="mailto:talmo@salk.edu">talmo@salk.edu</a>
    with your CV to discuss potential opportunities at any level.
  </p>

  <h3>Philosophy</h3>
  <p>
    A core belief in our lab is that being happy is essential to doing good science. We
    believe that your success is everyone's success, and therefore place an extremely
    high value on <strong>mentorship</strong>, <strong>work-life balance</strong> and
    <strong>open communication</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Lab members should expect to be able to <strong>ask for help whenever they need
    it</strong>, and be eager to pay it forward during their tenure here and beyond.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our group's culture is intended to reflect the reality that <strong>not everyone is
    afforded the same opportunities</strong> before they arrive here, but that that does
    not mean they are not as qualified or worthy of the chance to prove themselves. It is
    only by acknowledging the structural disparities that are inherent in academia that we
    can <strong>effect real change</strong> — and do amazing science along the way!
  </p>

  <h3>Location</h3>
  <p>
    Come work in sunny San Diego! The lab is located in the
    <a href="https://salk.edu">Salk Institute for Biological Studies</a>, a non-profit
    research institute right next to the University of California San Diego. Surfing
    before or after work is recommended, but not required.
  </p>

  <h3>Open positions</h3>
  <p>
    We do not currently have open positions. If you are interested in any of the roles
    below, feel free to reach out to chat about potential upcoming opportunities —
    <strong>we strongly recommend including your CV and GitHub</strong>.
  </p>

  <h4>Software engineers</h4>
  <p>
    We are always on the lookout for scientific programmers. If you have a background in
    DevOps, MLOps, web dev or other software engineering skillsets and an interest in deep
    learning and computer vision, we'd like to chat. Prior experience in machine learning
    research is not required — just show us your code. We offer very competitive
    compensation and are happy to provide training to prepare our engineers for a
    continuing career in research or engineering, in academia or industry.
  </p>

  <h4>Postdoctoral fellows</h4>
  <p>
    Finishing your PhD soon in neuroscience, computer science, physics, or another
    computational field? We regularly recruit postdocs to work directly with us or jointly
    with one of our collaborators.
  </p>

  <h4>Graduate students</h4>
  <p>
    If you are interested in pursuing a MS or PhD while working in the lab, you will need
    to apply to one of the graduate programs at UCSD. We are open to accepting students
    from any program, but we recommend
    <a href="https://neurograd.ucsd.edu/index.html">Neuroscience</a>,
    <a href="https://cogsci.ucsd.edu/graduates/phd-program/index.html">Cognitive Science</a>,
    <a href="https://datascience.ucsd.edu/academics/graduate/admissions/">Data Science</a>, or
    <a href="https://cse.ucsd.edu/graduate/degree-programs">Computer Science and Engineering</a>.
    If you have questions, aren't sure which program to apply to, or just want to chat
    about graduate school options, feel free to reach out.
  </p>

  <h4>High school and undergraduate internships</h4>
  <p>
    Interested in doing research with us during the school year or for a summer? We are
    always looking for talented undergraduates to take on ambitious independent research
    projects. You will be treated like a graduate student, but we will provide all the
    support and mentoring you need to meet our mutual expectations and succeed in
    transitioning to the next stage of your career.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>UCSD students</strong>: to work at Salk you will need to enroll in a research
    for academic credit course such as
    <a href="https://biology.ucsd.edu/education/undergrad/research/research-acad-cred/">BISP 199</a>,
    <a href="https://cogsci.ucsd.edu/undergraduates/student-resources/research.html">COGS 199</a> or
    <a href="https://cse.ucsd.edu/undergraduate/cse199-independent-study-undergraduates">CSE 199</a>.
    We especially recommend that students considering a longer stay apply for the
    <a href="https://ugresearch.ucsd.edu/research-programs/trels/index.html">Triton Research &amp; Experiential Learning Scholars (TRELS)</a>
    program, which provides funding to conduct and present your research.
  </p>
</section>

